cff-version: "1.2.0"
message: "If you use this repository, its white paper, or the six-layer application stack in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "Meaning Intelligence: Meta-Intelligence Theory and the Six-Layer Application Stack"
abstract: >-
  An open research and practice project on meta-intelligence: the directional regulation of other
  intelligent activities. The repository contains a bilingual (Chinese/English) white paper, a
  six-layer application stack (L1 cognitive load reduction, L2 experiential rendering, L3 meaning
  generation, L4 value assessment, L5 direction selection, L6 recursive reflection and review),
  the E0-E6 evidence level scheme, the H1-H18 testable hypothesis cards with preregistered
  falsification criteria, a theory failure matrix, and a demonstration system (MSI) built from
  Manim scenes and a single-file interactive HTML page. The project treats meta-intelligence as a
  testable scientific hypothesis rather than a philosophical thesis, and commits to marking or
  removing any module that reaches its preregistered failure threshold.
type: software
